<title>USA: Top gates of perishables exported through NY, May.</title>
<headline>Top gates of perishables exported through NY, May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands, the Dominican Republic and Israel kept their place as the top three sources for perishable cargo imported into New York's John F. Kennedy Airport during May, the U.S. Department of Agriculture said in a monthly report.</p>
<p>Most perishables from the Netherlands and Dominican Republic were forwarded to Canada whilst those from Israel stayed in the New York area or were shipped by truck out of state.</p>
<p>The top three exports of perishables in tonnes for each country to JFK in May compared with May 96 were:</p>
<p> Country of origin   COMMODITY    May '97	    May '96</p>
<p> The Netherlands	Tomato	1,195		568</p>
<p>			    Pepper	  502		346</p>
<p>			    Cichorium     197		133</p>
<p> Dominican Republic   Cucurbit	205		161</p>
<p>			    Eggplant	 99		110</p>
<p>			    Mango	    94		122</p>
<p> Israel		   Tomato	  129		 89</p>
<p>			    Melon	    10		  6</p>
<p>			    Basil	     7		  4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
